<%# One pool and the rules that fill it. Locals: `group` (BudgetPagePresenter::Group) and `band`
    (the account it sits in — the card is a row of that band's drag list).

    The header says how the pool is doing in the app's ONE row vocabulary
    (`HomeHelper#pool_status_label`, spec §4.4) — the same words, the same red, as Home and the
    distribution screen. A second vocabulary here would have two screens describe one envelope
    differently on the same afternoon.

    `priority` is stated because this page is where funding priority is set; the number is what
    decides who gets filled first when the money runs out, and dragging this card — or its ▲▼ —
    is what writes it. %>
<section class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded"
         data-pool-group="<%= group.pool.name %>"
         data-pool-id="<%= group.pool.id %>"
         data-app--budget-page--reorder-target="row"
         draggable="true"
         data-action="dragstart->app--budget-page--reorder#start
                      dragend->app--budget-page--reorder#finish">
  <div class="px-6 py-3 border-b border-gray-200 flex justify-between items-baseline gap-4">
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
      <%= render "reorder_controls", group: group, band: band %>
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900"><%= group.pool.name %></h3>
      <span class="text-xs text-gray-400">priority <%= group.priority %></span>
    </div>
    <%# BOTH SUFFIXES, and neither is optional here — which is now a property of the SHAPE rather
        than of this file remembering to pass them (see `shared/_pool_status`).

        `period_closed:` says WHICH PERIOD the figure belongs to, and a swept rate-rule envelope
        reading `$400.00 left · last period` on Home while this page reads `$400.00 left` for the
        same pool on the same afternoon is two screens describing one envelope differently. It
        rides off the status's own memoised calculator, so this page still builds exactly one
        calculator per pool.

        `changed_after_distributing:` is the same objection said about the other clause, and this
        page is the one that owed it most: a `behind` envelope is on Home AND here, and this is
        where the rule was edited. The row below is the very form the user changed — the clause
        names the act, on the screen the act happened on. Through the group, never a query of the
        partial's own: the period it compares against is `today`'s. Silent on every state but
        `:behind` (HomeHelper#pool_status_label owns that gate).

        This partial passed `period_closed:` and NOT `changed_after_distributing:` until 2c's
        whole-plan review; passing an OBJECT rather than two keywords is what makes the omission
        unwritable rather than merely absent. `· holds $X` rides on `Group#balance_clause?`. %>
    <%= render "shared/pool_status", row: group %>
  </div>

  <% group.rules.each do |rule| %>
    <%= render "rule_row", rule: rule %>
  <% end %>
</section>
